Stopping a waiting thread, by a stop or by taking its process, leaves it on the notification's waiters,
so a signal would wake a thread that is stopped, or has no process to run in,
and a destroy of the thread's pool would leave the ring leading into memory that is no longer a thread;
a notification queues only the threads waiting on it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a thread that does not wait lends
Report: queue holds a thread it is not for
Report: runnable thread waits on something
Witness: fuzz cores-waiter-stopped

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -680,7 +680,6 @@ static bool thread_stop(struct thread *t)
     }
 #endif
     if (t->state == THREAD_WAITING) {
-        unwait(t);
         t->frame.pc -= CALL_SIZE;
     }
     t->state = THREAD_STOPPED;
